<p>As attackers can quickly change spear phishing attachments, it is important to have adaptable defenses that include user awareness training and response procedures, behavior-based malware defenses on email systems, web access and endpoint systems, and finally sec ops playbooks for early detection and response against suspicious email attachments or other phishing techniques. For more information on how McAfee can protect against suspicious email attachments, review this <a href="https://www.mcafee.com/blogs/author/atr-operational-intelligence-team/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">additional blog post</a>.</p>
